{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-ef9e3f40d3e1d6c2550a","statement":"Let $P$ be a parabolic subset of $\\Delta$. Assume that there is a base $\\Sigma$ of $\\Delta$\nfor which $\\Delta^+(\\Sigma) \\setminus P$ is a finite set. Then\n\n- [(i)] There exists a base $\\Pi$ of $\\Delta$ such that $\\Delta^+(\\Pi) \\subset P$;\n\n- [(ii)] $P$ is a principal parabolic subset of $\\Delta$.","source_id":"arXiv:0904.0041","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"1e8ba18967d9908e2987fe70707a0e3d7eeabb03241fc8ad235e85857bcd3052","kind":"proposition","label":"Proposition 4","ref_key":"kac-moody","name":"","order":9,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.0041","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"a14448ebca79573d37a3bacc4abdcb445d514c88d4c650e891ad880c4e25d977","line":546,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:31+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":297,"math_hints":34}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:0904.0041","title":"Parabolic sets of roots","abstract":"We compare two combinatorial definitions of parabolic sets of roots. We show that these definitions are equivalent for simple finite dimensional Lie algebras, affine Lie algebras, and toroidal Lie algebras. In contrast, these definitions are not always equivalent for simple finite dimensional Lie superalgebras.","authors":["Ivan Dimitrov","Vyacheslav Futorny","Dimitar Grantcharov"],"year":"2009","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.0041","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"gg":"\\mathfrak{g}","gh":"\\mathfrak{h}","gl":"\\mathfrak{l}","gn":"\\mathfrak{n}","gp":"\\mathfrak{p}","gs":"\\mathfrak{s}","C":"\\mathbb{C}","R":"\\mathbb{R}","Z":"\\mathbb{Z}","cT":"\\mathcal{T}","vep":"\\varepsilon","Hom":"\\operatorname{Hom}","Ker":"\\operatorname{Ker}","Span":"\\operatorname{Span}","Img":"\\operatorname{Im}","supp"